{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-categorical-fourier-transform-properties","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:categorical-fourier-transform-properties","kind":"remark","title":"Realisations of the categorical Fourier transform: Peter--Weyl, Wick rotation, and base rings","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-fourier","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-laplace","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-tannaka-krein-reconstruction","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-laplace-fourier-wick-rotation"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-fourier","tags":["hopf-algebra","grouplike","monoidal-functor","fourier","peter-weyl","tannakian"],"text":"categorical-fourier-transform-properties.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:categorical-fourier-transform-properties\"></a><p>When <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G = \\mathrm{SU}_q(2)</code>, the Tannaka--Krein reconstruction identifies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{F}</code> with the Peter--Weyl decomposition. Applying <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{F}</code> to the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat equation diagonalises the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Laplacian on each Peter--Weyl summand, producing the Peter--Weyl heat kernel. The algebraic Fourier transform via Peter--Weyl projection functions identically over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{F}_p</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Q}_p</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}[q, q^{-1}]</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-transform-properties.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.20.12"}
